<title>BELGIUM: EU daily wheat tax set to be adopted on Wednesday.</title>
<headline>EU daily wheat tax set to be adopted on Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is expected on Wednesday to override French opposition and approve a tax on daily exports of wheat grain and flour, Commission sources said.</p>
<p>The proposed tax of 15 Ecus a tonne on soft wheat grain and 20 Ecus on wheat flour exports was suspended last week after French EU Commissioner Edith Cresson objected.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, I think it will now go through,&quot; said one source, speaking after the issue had been discussed by the EU commissioners' aides.  </p>
<p>Previously unanimity was required because the proposal had been submitted under the so-called written procedure. Now it only requires a simple majority.</p>
<p>Cresson argued that the tax, which is aimed at saving scarce supplies for domestic consumers, was no longer needed because EU prices were falling.</p>
<p>But sources said that the fall was partly due to expectations of the tax.</p>
<p>Trade sources added that the week's delay had enabled nearly all exporters with special &quot;nil-value&quot; export licences to customs clear their grain. They would therefore not be liable to pay the tax.</p>
<p>--Brussels bureau +322 287 6830</p>
